    "fail_type": "compile_error",
    "problem_statement": "ostest's signal tests (sighand.c, posixtimer.c) compare signal sets as a scalar (oldset != allsigs and (uintmax_t)oldset) and the test needs a helper to compare sigset_t objects and a kernel print macro for them. The kernel represents sigset_t as an array of uint32_t (with _SIGSET_NELEM elements, accessed via _elem[]) and provides SIGSET_FMT/SIGSET_ELEM. The updated apps test must use the array-based sigset_t (sigset_isequal() and the SIGSET_FMT/SIGSET_ELEM macros) so it compiles and behaves correctly; it cannot build against a kernel where sigset_t is a plain uint32_t and those symbols/macros are absent.",
